  "minimum_safe_summary": "This empirical study investigated daylighting performance and energy implications in 35 Hong Kong office buildings, with detailed simulations of two typical blocks using RADIANCE. Key findings indicate that about one-third of perimeter office areas achieve an average daylight factor of 5%, and proper daylight-linked lighting controls could save over 25% of electric lighting energy. Daylighting performance is significantly influenced by window area, glass type, external obstructions, and room depth, with DFs rapidly decreasing away from windows and at lower floors. Glare indices were generally below discomfort thresholds. The study concludes that current building fa\u00e7ade designs are conducive to effective daylighting, offering substantial energy savings. No explicit limitations were stated.",
